Summary: Don't let the main thread and a GL thread change an OpenGL context's view at once
Category: graphics
Kind: fix
Origin: wine-mac-builds
  Version: 11.22
  Changes: 10.0 passes opaque macdrv_opengl_context and macdrv_view handles,
    cast inside each function
Upstream: no; the code is the same in WineHQ 10.0 to master and CrossOver
 26.3.0 (checked 2026-11-25).
Why: A WineOpenGLContext's view, latent view and update flags are changed
 by the GL threads (macdrv_make_context_current, macdrv_update_opengl_context)
 and, for contexts added while their view wasn't drawable, by the main thread
 in the content view's viewWillDraw, which calls
 macdrv_update_opengl_context. Nothing serialises the two. Both can read the
 same old view or latent view and release it, and the view is then released
 once too often. Give each context a recursive lock, held around those
 changes. The GL thread can hold it while it waits for the main thread
 (OnMainThread), so viewWillDraw only tries the lock. If it's busy, the
 context stays pending and the view asks to be drawn again. The lock is
 per context because a GL thread waiting in OnMainThread handles window
 queries, which run the program's window procedure (WM_GETMINMAXINFO at
 a resize or fullscreen change, WM_RENDERFORMAT, OLE drops), and that can
 wait for another thread. With one lock for every context, that other
 thread could be stuck taking the lock for its own context, and neither
 would return. opengl32 lets a context be current on one thread at a
 time and not be deleted while current, so only that thread and the main
 thread take a context's lock. (updateGLContexts still sets the flags on
 the main thread without it; that can only lose an update, not release
 twice.)
 It needs a GL context made current on a view that isn't drawable yet,
 which Wine 11's framebuffer GL surfaces (EmulateModeset) cause when two
 threads draw to one window: each gets its own surface and view.
 A winemac instrumented to count threads inside each context's functions
 found about 40 such overlaps in 15 s of a stress program (two render
 threads switching between two windows), all viewWillDraw's update during
 a GL thread's, and none with this patch.
 It came out of the hunt for a crash at objc_release+34 in Nancy Drew games
 ("Pattern A"), which turned out to be another bug
 (winemac-gl-context-dealloc-off-main-thread).
Programs: none known; programs that draw to one window from two threads
 with EmulateModeset on (Wine 11)
Uncertain: whether any program hits the double release: the stress program
 shows the overlap but never crashed, and no crash has been traced to it.
 The deadlock the per-context lock avoids was found by reading, not seen.
Related: winemac-gl-update-on-main-thread,
 winemac-gl-context-dealloc-off-main-thread; the same viewWillDraw and GL
 thread interplay
No test: timing only: the stress program shows two threads overlapping,
 but the crash needs a narrower interleaving than it reaches, and the
 deadlock a window query that arrives while a GL thread waits for the
 main thread
Status: 10.0: 2026-11-26: a lock per context instead of one for all.
 The one-lock version passed the suite in build7 and
 in two quick builds; no games run.
 10.0: 2026-11-26: quick 20261126T044550 (macOS 26.7.2, M1 Max): the
 regression suite passed (GL and window tests in a GUI session); smoke
 stopped at its audio step, which failed for every build and for afplay
 while meeka's audio output was wedged.
 10.0: 2026-11-26: quick 20261126T072237 (macOS 26.7.2, M1 Max): the
 smoke test passed, sound included, once a pending microphone prompt
 was answered.

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_opengl.m b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_opengl.m
index 4a6ae6f..fe516ec 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_opengl.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_opengl.m
@@ -26,14 +26,32 @@
 #include "cocoa_app.h"
 #include "cocoa_event.h"
 
+#include <pthread.h>
+
 #pragma GCC diagnostic ignored "-Wdeclaration-after-statement"
 
 
 @interface WineOpenGLContext ()
+{
+    /* Held while this context's view, latent view and update flags change.
+     * The GL thread the context is current on changes them in
+     * macdrv_make_context_current() and macdrv_update_opengl_context(), and
+     * the main thread in the content view's viewWillDraw. Without it both
+     * could swap the same view at once and release it twice. The GL thread
+     * can hold it while it waits for the main thread, so the main thread
+     * only ever tries to take it. It's per context: a lock shared by all
+     * contexts would make one GL thread wait for another, which can wait
+     * for the first (a paste or drop query it's handling in OnMainThread). */
+    pthread_mutex_t changeLock;
+}
+
 @property (retain, nonatomic) NSView* latentView;
 
     + (NSView*) dummyView;
     - (void) wine_updateBackingSize:(const CGSize*)size;
+    - (void) lockChanges;
+    - (BOOL) tryLockChanges;
+    - (void) unlockChanges;
 
 @end
 
@@ -41,10 +59,26 @@
 @implementation WineOpenGLContext
 @synthesize latentView, needsUpdate, needsReattach;
 
+    - (instancetype) initWithCGLContextObj:(CGLContextObj)context
+    {
+        self = [super initWithCGLContextObj:context];
+        if (self)
+        {
+            pthread_mutexattr_t attr;
+
+            pthread_mutexattr_init(&attr);
+            pthread_mutexattr_settype(&attr, PTHREAD_MUTEX_RECURSIVE);
+            pthread_mutex_init(&changeLock, &attr);
+            pthread_mutexattr_destroy(&attr);
+        }
+        return self;
+    }
+
     - (void) dealloc
     {
         [[self view] release];
         [latentView release];
+        pthread_mutex_destroy(&changeLock);
         [super dealloc];
     }
 
@@ -167,6 +201,21 @@
         [self clearDrawable];
     }
 
+    - (void) lockChanges
+    {
+        pthread_mutex_lock(&changeLock);
+    }
+
+    - (BOOL) tryLockChanges
+    {
+        return !pthread_mutex_trylock(&changeLock);
+    }
+
+    - (void) unlockChanges
+    {
+        pthread_mutex_unlock(&changeLock);
+    }
+
     - (void) removeFromViews:(BOOL)removeViews
     {
         if ([self view])
@@ -219,7 +268,9 @@ void macdrv_dispose_opengl_context(macdrv_opengl_context c)
 {
     WineOpenGLContext *context = (WineOpenGLContext*)c;
 
+    [context lockChanges];
     [context removeFromViews:YES];
+    [context unlockChanges];
     [context release];
 }
 }
@@ -236,6 +287,7 @@ void macdrv_make_context_current(macdrv_opengl_context c, macdrv_view v, CGRect
 
     if (context && view)
     {
+        [context lockChanges];
         if (view == [context view] || view == [context latentView])
         {
             [context wine_updateBackingSize:&r.size];
@@ -267,6 +319,7 @@ void macdrv_make_context_current(macdrv_opengl_context c, macdrv_view v, CGRect
         }
 
         [context makeCurrentContext];
+        [context unlockChanges];
     }
     else
     {
@@ -276,11 +329,19 @@ void macdrv_make_context_current(macdrv_opengl_context c, macdrv_view v, CGRect
         {
             [WineOpenGLContext clearCurrentContext];
             if (currentContext != context)
+            {
+                [currentContext lockChanges];
                 [currentContext removeFromViews:YES];
+                [currentContext unlockChanges];
+            }
         }
 
         if (context)
+        {
+            [context lockChanges];
             [context removeFromViews:YES];
+            [context unlockChanges];
+        }
     }
 }
 }
@@ -294,6 +355,7 @@ void macdrv_update_opengl_context(macdrv_opengl_context c)
 {
     WineOpenGLContext *context = (WineOpenGLContext*)c;
 
+    [context lockChanges];
     if (context.needsUpdate)
     {
         BOOL reattach = context.needsReattach;
@@ -327,7 +389,25 @@ void macdrv_update_opengl_context(macdrv_opengl_context c)
             [context resetSurfaceIfBackingSizeChanged];
         }
     }
+    [context unlockChanges];
+}
 }
+
+/***********************************************************************
+ *              macdrv_try_update_opengl_context
+ *
+ * For the main thread: updates the context unless a GL thread is changing
+ * it, and returns whether it did.
+ */
+int macdrv_try_update_opengl_context(macdrv_opengl_context c)
+{
+    WineOpenGLContext *context = (WineOpenGLContext*)c;
+
+    if (![context tryLockChanges]) return 0;
+    context.needsUpdate = TRUE;
+    macdrv_update_opengl_context(c);
+    [context unlockChanges];
+    return 1;
 }
 
 /***********************************************************************
diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
index 68de265..cb2b2f5 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_window.m
@@ -585,13 +585,20 @@ static CVReturn WineDisplayLinkCallback(CVDisplayLinkRef displayLink, const CVTi
     {
         [super viewWillDraw];
 
-        for (WineOpenGLContext* context in pendingGlContexts)
+        for (WineOpenGLContext* context in [[pendingGlContexts copy] autorelease])
         {
-            context.needsUpdate = TRUE;
-            macdrv_update_opengl_context((macdrv_opengl_context)context);
+            /* A GL thread is changing it; leave it pending for the next draw. */
+            if (!macdrv_try_update_opengl_context((macdrv_opengl_context)context))
+                continue;
+            [glContexts addObject:context];
+            [pendingGlContexts removeObjectIdenticalTo:context];
+        }
+        if ([pendingGlContexts count])
+        {
+            dispatch_async(dispatch_get_main_queue(), ^{
+                [self setNeedsDisplay:YES];
+            });
         }
-        [glContexts addObjectsFromArray:pendingGlContexts];
-        [pendingGlContexts removeAllObjects];
     }
 
     - (void) addGLContext:(WineOpenGLContext*)context
